# LIN-AGENT-RUNTIME-008: Causal Path Expansion & Explicit Topological Frontier

## 1. Object & Scientific Mandate
Following `LIN-AGENT-RUNTIME-007` (which demonstrated that passive cumulative scoring collapses at depths $D_3, D_4, D_5$):
> **Does Explicit Causal Frontier Expansion ($\text{Frontier}_{t+1} = \text{Callees}(\text{Refuted}_t) \cup \text{TransitiveLeaves}$) allow the agent to successfully traverse deep causal chains ($D_3 \rightarrow D_5$) and improve deep root-cause localization accuracy compared to passive re-ranking?**

---

## 2. Explicit Causal Frontier Mechanism

```text
At t=0: Entry Node A (Symptom)
        │
    [TEST FAIL] -> Refute A
        │
At t=1: Frontier_1 = Direct Callees(A) -> { B }
        Prompt explicitly presents: Causal Path [A -> B]
        │
    [TEST FAIL] -> Refute B
        │
At t=2: Frontier_2 = Direct Callees(B) -> { C, D, E }
        Topological Leaf Ranking: Prioritize leaf utility E
        Prompt explicitly presents: Causal Path [A -> B -> C -> D -> E]
        │
    [TEST PASS] -> Verified Root Cause in Leaf E
```

---

## 3. Evaluated Arms across $D_1..D_5$
- **Arm A (RAW):** Zero-state baseline.
- **Arm B (CHAT):** Textual error history buffer.
- **Arm C1 (LIN Cumulative):** Passive score boost from `RUNTIME-007`.
- **Arm C2 (LIN Causal Frontier):** Explicit directional path expansion down the DAG.
